{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--awa-akusu-distribution-variation","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--akusu-awa-variation"],"statement":{"en":"The conjunctive particle awa expresses a similar sequential meaning to akusu, but its frequency varies across dialects and genres.","ja":"接続助詞 awa は akusu と同様の継起的な意味を表すが、その使用頻度には方言差やジャンル差がある。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["awa","akusu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0342-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--awa-akusu-saru-register-split","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--akusu-awa-variation"],"statement":{"en":"In Saru Ainu, awa is predominantly used in verse, whereas akusu is used for the same sequential function in prose tales.","ja":"沙流方言では、韻文において主として awa が用いられるのに対し、散文説話では同様の状況に akusu が用いられる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["awa","akusu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0342-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--awa-akusu-distribution-variation","differs_in":"scope","note":"specifies the verse vs prose register split in Saru"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--horobetsu-awa-frequency","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--akusu-awa-variation"],"statement":{"en":"In Horobetsu Ainu, the conjunctive particle awa is overwhelmingly more frequent than akusu.","ja":"幌別方言では、接続助詞 awa が akusu よりも圧倒的に多く用いられる。"},"type":"frequency","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/horobetsu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["awa","akusu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0342-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--awa-akusu-distribution-variation","differs_in":"scope","note":"specifies Horobetsu preference for awa"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--shizunai-tokachi-akusu-frequency","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--akusu-awa-variation"],"statement":{"en":"In Shizunai and Tokachi Ainu, akusu is used more frequently than awa.","ja":"静内方言および十勝方言では、awa よりも akusu のほうが多く用いられる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai","doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["akusu","awa"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0342-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--awa-akusu-distribution-variation","differs_in":"scope","note":"specifies Shizunai and Tokachi preference for akusu"},{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--horobetsu-awa-frequency","differs_in":"dialect","note":"Horobetsu prefers awa whereas Shizunai and Tokachi prefer akusu"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--akusu-result-without-causality","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--akusu-awa"],"statement":{"en":"The conjunctive particle akusu connects an event that occurred in connection with the result of a prior occurrence, without requiring any causal relationship.","ja":"接続助詞 akusu は先行事象の結果に関連して生じた後続事案を接続し、因果関係の有無を問わない。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["akusu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0342-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--akus-unexpected-development","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--akusu-awa"],"statement":{"en":"In Shizunai Ainu, akus marks a background clause into which a new and unexpected event is introduced, or an action followed by a surprising development.","ja":"静内方言において、akus は新規かつ予期せぬ事象が導入される背景節、あるいは驚くべき展開が続く動作を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["akus"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0242-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--akusu-result-without-causality","differs_in":"framework","note":"unexpectedness and discovery account vs non-causal resultative account"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--hine-folktale-frequency","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--hine"],"statement":{"en":"In Shizunai Ainu, hine tends to occur more frequently in folktales than in everyday colloquial speech.","ja":"静内方言において、hine は日常会話よりも昔話において頻度が高い傾向がある。"},"type":"frequency","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["hine"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0236-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--hine-prose-tale-opening-frequency","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--hine"],"statement":{"en":"In Hokkaido Ainu prose tales, hine is frequently used at the beginning of the narrative to describe the narrator's personal circumstances.","ja":"北海道アイヌ語の散文説話において、語り手の人物像を描く冒頭部で hine が多用される。"},"type":"frequency","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"asserted","conditions":["narrative opening of prose tales"]},"forms":["hine"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0335-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--hine-folktale-frequency","differs_in":"scope","note":"identifies the narrative opening as the specific folktale locus where hine clusters"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--hine-chronological-sequencing","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--hine"],"statement":{"en":"The conjunctive particle hine is used simply to arrange events in chronological order.","ja":"接続助詞 hine は単に時間的な経過順に出来事を並べるときに用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["hine","hinne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0335-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--hine-sequential-meaning","differs_in":"level-of-analysis","note":"articulates the chronological ordering function behind the basic connective gloss"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--hine-sequential-meaning","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--hine"],"statement":{"en":"The conjunctive particle hine functions to connect clauses with the meaning 'and then / having done...'.","ja":"接続助詞 hine は「〜て」を意味し、先行節に続いて出来事を接続する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["hine"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0385-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--eastern-hine-distribution-tamura","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--hine-form"],"statement":{"en":"In Eastern Hokkaido varieties, hine is substantially less frequent than wa or tek in Shiranuka, Kushiro has ine, and Honbetsu Tokachi lacks hine or ine.","ja":"東部方言において、白糠方言の hine は wa や tek より格段に少なく、釧路方言は ine を持ち、十勝本別方言は hine も ine も使用しないとされる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/northeast/kushiro","doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"reported","conditions":[]},"forms":["hine","ine","wa","tek"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0335-05","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--tokachi-hinne-and-hine-distribution","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--hine-form"],"statement":{"en":"In Tokachi Ainu, hinne corresponds to hine and functions identically, while hine is also used in varieties outside Honbetsu.","ja":"十勝方言では hinne が hine に相当して同様に用いられ、本別以外の方言では hine も使用される。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"asserted","conditions":[]},"forms":["hinne","hine"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0335-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--eastern-hine-distribution-tamura","differs_in":"scope","note":"clarifies the presence of hinne and non-Honbetsu hine in Tokachi"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--while-there-is-usually-no-interdependence-between-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--akusu-awa"],"statement":{"en":"While there is usually no interdependence between the events linked by akus, in a few cases the conjunctionalized clause may function as the cause or condition for the occurrence of the following clause.","ja":"akusで結ばれた2つの述語の事象間には通常相互依存関係はないが、前節が後節の事象の生起の原因または条件とみなされる場合がわずかにある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["akus"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0242-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--akusu-functions-as-a-conjunctive-particle-meaning-when","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--akusu-awa"],"statement":{"en":"akusu functions as a conjunctive particle meaning 'when' or 'but'.","ja":"akusu は「〜と，〜が」を意味する接続助詞として機能する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["akusu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0383-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--the-conjunctions-ike-hike-aike-ahike-singular-akusu","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--akusu-awa-variation"],"statement":{"en":"The conjunctions ike, hike, aike, ahike, singular akusu, and plural rokkusu are equivalent in meaning to awa.","ja":"ike, hike, aike, ahike, 単数 akusu, 複数 rokkusu は awa と同義である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ike","hike","aike","ahike","akusu","rokkusu","awa"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0162-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--in-the-ishikari-dialect-akusu-is-limited-in","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--akusu-awa-variation"],"statement":{"en":"In the Ishikari dialect, akusu is limited in use and awa is more frequent.","ja":"石狩方言では akusu は限られていて awa が多い。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/ishikari"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["akusu","awa"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0342-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--the-conjunction-hine-is-equivalent-in-meaning-to","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topics":["topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference","topic:complex/hine-akusu-switch-reference--hine"],"statement":{"en":"The conjunction hine is equivalent in meaning to wa.","ja":"接続助詞 hine は wa と同義である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["hine","wa"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0160-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
